# Code owners.
#
# Every line here is a real fact about who owns the code, not a placeholder.
# `sddk knowledge scan` quarantines any file with no declared owner, because
# knowledge nobody is accountable for is knowledge nobody reviews. On a public
# repository the same reasoning applies to code: an unowned path is a path
# nobody is obliged to keep safe.
#
# The signed specification pack is imported verbatim and must never be edited in
# place, so it is listed here explicitly rather than inherited from a wildcard.

# Default owner for everything not matched below.
*                               @Rubentxu

# The normative spec pack: owned, but changes are a deliberate act, not a
# drive-by fix. A defect in it is recorded and gated, never patched silently.
agent-secretless-vault-spec/    @Rubentxu

# The adversarial harness is the project's evidence. A change here can turn a
# red result green without the product changing, so it is held to the same
# standard as the code it measures.
tests/adversarial/              @Rubentxu

# Verification evidence. These are records of what was observed; editing one
# retroactively is falsification, not documentation.
docs/receipts/                  @Rubentxu
